tiva Palmeiras\"). Stripped from the start.\n+_LEGAL_PREFIXES = (\n+    \"sociedade esportiva\", \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\",\n+    \"club de regatas\", \"clube de regatas\", \"grêmio recreativo\",\n+    \"club atletico\", \"clube atletico\", \"atletico clube\",\n+)\n+\n+# Phrases that may appear as a *trailing* suffix (e.g. \"Corinthians Sport\n+# Club\", \"Boavista S/A\"). Stripped from the end.\n _LEGAL_SUFFIXES = (\n-    \"sport club\", \"sociedade esportiva\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\",\n-    \"club de regatas\", \"club atletico\", \"atletico clube\", \"grêmio\",\n-    \"s/a\", \"sa\", \"fc\", \"sc\", \"ac\", \"ec\", \"aa\",\n+    \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\", \"club de regatas\",\n+    \"club atletico\", \"atletico clube\", \"s/a\", \"sa\", \"fc\", \"sc\", \"ac\", \"ec\", \"aa\",\n )\n \n # A parenthetical such as \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\" that appears in\n # the Copa do Brasil dataset.\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-862dd344e70f/normalizer.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-862dd344e70f/normalizer.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-862dd344e70f/normalizer.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-862dd344e70f/normalizer.py\n@@ -41,12 +41,21 @@\n     # South American country tags seen in Libertadores dataset\n     \"URU\",\"EQU\",\"ARG\",\"CHI\",\"PAR\",\"BOL\",\"COL\",\"PER\",\"VEN\",\"MEX\",\"ECU\",\n }\n \n+# Phrases that may appear as a *leading* prefix of a club's full legal\n+# name (e.g. \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\"). Stripped from the start.\n+_LEGAL_PREFIXES = (\n+    \"sociedade esportiva\", \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\",\n+    \"club de regatas\", \"clube de regatas\", \"grêmio recreativo\",\n+    \"club atletico\", \"clube atletico\", \"atletico clube\",\n+)\n+\n+# Phrases that may appear as a *trailing* suffix (e.g. \"Corinthians Sport\n+# Club\", \"Boavista S/A\"). Stripped from the end.\n _LEGAL_SUFFIXES = (\n-    \"sport club\", \"sociedade esportiva\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\",\n-    \"club de regatas\", \"club atletico\", \"atletico clube\", \"grêmio\",\n-    \"s/a\", \"sa\", \"fc\", \"sc\", \"ac\", \"ec\", \"aa\",\n+    \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\", \"club de regatas\",\n+    \"club atletico\", \"atletico clube\", \"s/a\", \"sa\", \"fc\", \"sc\", \"ac\", \"ec\", \"aa\",\n )\n \n # A parenthetical such as \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\" that appears in\n # the Copa do Brasil dataset.\n","additions":12,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"normalizer.py","time":{"start":1788201276848,"end":1788201276851}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two issues with the normalizer:\n1. \"Grêmio-RS\" → the suffix strip removes \"-RS\" but then the trailing legal suffix \"grêmio\" matches? No, lowered = \"grêmio\". It checks `_LEGAL_SUFFIXES` which includes \"grêmio\" — that's wrong, \"Grêmio\" is a team name, not a legal suffix. I added \"grêmio\" to legal suffixes incorrectly. Let me remove it.\n\n2. \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\" — \"esportiva\" isn't in legal suffixes, and \"sociedade esportiva\" is in legal suffixes. The loop removes \"sociedade esportiva\" only if the string ends with \" sociedade esportiva\". But here it starts with it. So it doesn't get stripped. The issue: I need to handle leading prefixes too. Actually, \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\" — the canonical should be \"Palmeiras\". \n\nFor the spec's full-name example: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" should be \"Corinthians Paulista\"? Or \"Corinthias\"? The spec mentions \"Full names: 'Sport Club Corinthians Paulista'\". Hmm. The reasonable canonical is to strip \"Sport Club\" prefix.\n\nLet me reconsider. The legal suffix list should be prefixes/suffixes that appear anywhere as standalone tokens and get removed. Let me change the approach: tokenize and filter out tokens that are in a stopword set.\n\nStopword tokens: sport, club, esporte, clube, esportiva, sociedade, futebol, atletico, regatas, paulista, etc. But \"atletico\" is part of \"Atlético-MG\" team name... and \"Paulista\" is part of \"Corinthians Paulista\". Hmm, this is getting tricky.\n\nActually for the test I wrote, I want \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\" → \"Palmeiras\". Let me just strip leading \"Sociedade Esportiva \" and similar leading prefixes, plus trailing legal suffixes.\n\nLet me simplify: define a set of prefix phrases to strip from the start, and a set of suffix phrases to strip from the end. Remove \"grêmio\" from legal suffixes (it's a team name).\n\nPrefixes to strip (case-insensitive): \"Sociedade Esportiva \", \"Sport Club \", \"Esporte Clube \", \"Futebol Clube \", \"Club de Regatas \", \"Clube de Regatas \", \"Grêmio Recreativo \".\n\nSuffixes to strip: \" Sport Club\", \" Esporte Clube\", \" Futebol Clube\", \" S/A\", \" SA\", \" FC\", \" SC\", \" EC\", \" AA\", \" AC\".\n\nActually a token-filter approach is cleaner. Let me define stopword tokens to remove anywhere: {sport, club, clube, esporte, esportiva, sociedade, futebol, de, regatas, recreativo, atletico, athletico}. But \"atletico\" as stopword would turn \"Atlético-MG\" → \"mg\" which is wrong.\n\nThis is genuinely ambiguous. The key thing the tests need: Palmeiras variants unify. Let me make the test cases align with a reasonable normalization rather than over-engineering.\n\nLet me reconsider my own test. test_same_team_same_key asserts:\n- name_key(\"Palmeiras-SP\") == \"palmeiras\" ✓\n- name_key(\"Palmeiras\") == \"palmeiras\" ✓\n- name_key(\"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\") should == \"palmeiras\"\n\nFor the third to work, I need to strip \"Sociedade Esportiva \" prefix.\n\nFor Grêmio: remove \"grêmio\" from legal suffixes. \"Grêmio-RS\" → strip \"-RS\" → \"Grêmio\". \n\nLet me rewrite the canonical_name to:\n1. Drop parentheticals\n2. Strip -UF/-country suffix\n3. Strip leading legal-prefix phrases\n4. Strip trailing legal-suffix phrases\n5. Collapse whitespace\n\nAnd keep accents.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591a159f001ujseCNGW0RGAwA","sessionID":"ses_fa6ebaa84ffeZXZBHmklmgLhAK","messageID":"msg_05919c2260010pvz6eZ9DB4nmx"}}
