{"type":"text","timestamp":1788201343679,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ebaa84ffeZXZBHmklmgLhAK","part":{"id":"prt_0591b07ad001tW4jLDT8ruDEPr","messageID":"msg_0591aff35001pMkskMSjZN2AMn","sessionID":"ses_fa6ebaa84ffeZXZBHmklmgLhAK","type":"text","text":"Done. All 52 BDD tests pass and the MCP server builds and runs.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a Brazilian Soccer MCP server per `TASK.md`:\n\n- **`normalizer.py`** — canonicalizes team names across the six datasets (strips `-SP`/` - RJ`/`-EQU` suffixes, leading `Sociedade Esportiva`/`Sport Club` prefixes, trailing legal suffixes, parentheticals; accent-preserving display + accent-folded equality keys).\n- **`data_loader.py`** — stdlib-`csv` loader unifying all 6 files into one `SoccerData` object (23,954 matches + 18,207 players), with multi-format date parsing (ISO, ISO+time, Brazilian DD/MM/YYYY), robust goal coercion, and team/season indexes.\n- **`analysis.py`** — query engine: match search, head-to-head, team stats, computed standings, champion/relegated, biggest wins, avg goals, best home record, derbies, player search.\n- **`server.py`** — FastMCP server exposing 13 tools (one per spec capability).\n- **`tests/`** — 52 BDD Given/When/Then scenarios covering normalizer, loader, analysis, and server.\n- **`README.md`** updated.\n\nVerification: 2019 Brasileirão champion correctly computed as Flamengo; Fla-Flu H2H = 31 Flamengo wins; avg 2.51 goals/match; all success criteria met.","time":{"start":1788201338797,"end":1788201343676}}}
